For the five relations on $NN$ sharing a final digit, $<$, $!=$, equality to $1$ on both sides, and $abs(a - b) <= 3$: the final-digit relation and $abs(a - b) <= 3$ are reflexive and symmetric, though only the former is transitive; $<$ is transitive only; $!=$ is symmetric only; and $a R b$ exactly when $a = b = 1$ is transitive only. Only the final-digit relation satisfies all three properties.
